Core/Jessie: God, the smell when I get close to them…
Core/Rose: Decomposition mixed with plant matter. Rotting mulch.
Core/Jessie: That’s exactly what it is. How do you know?
Core/Rose: I’ve been close too. When I had to leave the lab for supplies.
Core/Jessie: You went out there alone?
Core/Rose: Didn’t have a choice.
Core/Jessie: You’re tougher than you sound on the radio.
Core/Rose: I have to be.